# apps/api/Dockerfile's build context is the repo root. Docker does NOT read
# .gitignore — this file needs its own complete exclusion list. Two goals:
# (1) no secret/credential material ever enters an image layer, (2) keep the context
# (and Docker's build cache) free of large, host-specific, or irrelevant state.
#
# Keep the "credential files" patterns scoped (never a blanket *.json) — package.json,
# package-lock.json, every workspace's package.json, and tsconfig*.json are required by
# `npm ci` and the TypeScript build.

# Version control
.git
.github

# Installed/build output — reinstalled and regenerated fresh inside the image
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/out-tsc
**/test-output
**/coverage
.nx

# Prisma's generated client — produced fresh by `prisma generate` inside the build
# stage; a host-generated copy could be stale or built for the wrong platform.
libs/database/src/generated

# Env files — real values live outside the image (Cloud Run env vars / secrets), never
# baked in.
.env*

# Credential files — scoped patterns only. These do NOT catch GCP's actual default
# service-account key download filename ({project-id}-{random-hex}.json) — the real
# guarantee against shipping one is structural: with GCS_CLIENT_EMAIL/GCS_PRIVATE_KEY
# unset, production reads no keyfile at all (see StorageService). Never save a
# downloaded service-account key file inside this repo; set the two env vars directly
# in `.env` instead.
*-key.json
*.key.json
*service-account*.json
*.keyfile.json
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Local Claude Code state — never relevant to a container build
.claude

# Docs — unread by the build; excluding them stops an unrelated README/ARCHITECTURE
# edit from invalidating the `COPY . .` layer's cache
*.md
